--TEST--
An unterminated html template is `E0002`, named at the backtick that opened it rather than at the end of the file — `rule:core-classes/html-template`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The template adds no diagnostic of its own: `E0002` is the code an
// unterminated string, heredoc and interpolation already carry, and a fourth
// code for a fourth delimiter would be three spellings of one mistake.
// What matters is the span — a run to end of file is only useful if it names
// where the run started.
var $open = html`<p>never closed;
echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0002]: unterminated html template
  --> case.nvs:7:13
%A
